+- A monotonically increasing instruction ID is used to detect and prevent stale operand usage, matching ROB logic functionally without identical bounds wrapping.
+- Invalidation logic surrounding mispredict recovery paths is dead code; the predictor observes only correctly squashed trace execution.
+- The correction term operates entirely asynchronously of internal TAGE thresholding, losing coupling capability.
+- The host does not differentiate between FP16, FP32, and FP64 register writes. The port implements the FP64 digest variant for all floating point registers.
+- The port plan specifies compile_time_define bindings for parameters but does not include a hook point to modify the Makefile to pass these defines to the compiler. This will prevent the search from successfully varying parameters.
